WEBVTT

01:30.740 --> 01:34.370
EPISODE 8: THE SECRET OF THE CROW

01:35.070 --> 01:38.080
Goriki Ryoga? What are you doing here?!

01:38.600 --> 01:40.580
Long time no see, Ogawara.

01:40.980 --> 01:44.450
I'm not here to start anything. 
I'm only taking him back.

01:45.240 --> 01:49.130
With our relics all busted up, 
we couldn't fight anyway.

01:49.130 --> 01:50.840
Don't make me laugh!

01:52.910 --> 01:56.520
If that's how you're gonna be, 
I guess I have no choice.

01:57.320 --> 02:00.930
The bodyguards about to attack us

02:00.930 --> 02:04.150
shall suffer the agony of death.

02:04.450 --> 02:07.510
And the source of the pain is once again...

02:13.120 --> 02:14.280
their crown jewels.

02:21.700 --> 02:24.670
What? You tricked me!

02:25.040 --> 02:28.610
How am I supposed to restore 
all these in three days?!

02:28.990 --> 02:30.420
Do you ever stop whining?

02:30.750 --> 02:33.350
They look like they'll fall 
apart if you so much as

02:33.350 --> 02:34.930
look at them wrong!

02:35.510 --> 02:37.550
Quit complaining and get started!

02:37.550 --> 02:40.560
And watch your tone. I'm your boss.

02:40.560 --> 02:45.390
I mean... restorations 
aren't that easy, okay?

02:45.390 --> 02:50.270
This amount will easily 
take me several months.

02:50.270 --> 02:52.200
Don't exaggerate.

02:52.200 --> 02:54.280
Is this your restoration relic?

02:54.630 --> 02:57.070
The Japanese Ukiyo-e Painter Brush.

02:58.870 --> 03:02.290
Try it yourself, and you'll see 
whether I'm exaggerating or not.

03:03.350 --> 03:04.550
You sure?

03:08.440 --> 03:13.550
See? It's not like anyone can do it 
just because they have the brush.

03:13.910 --> 03:17.550
I'll bet a year's salary 
that you could never...

03:19.930 --> 03:22.110
Th-That can't be right!

03:22.110 --> 03:25.940
How'd you do that so easily?! 
And so quickly, too!

03:26.350 --> 03:29.940
Well, looks like I won the bet.
What're you gonna do now?

03:30.320 --> 03:33.590
Why do you even need me, then?

03:33.590 --> 03:35.280
Just do it all yourself!

03:35.670 --> 03:37.920
I'm not the right guy. See?

03:40.710 --> 03:45.040
What is this rampant dominance? 
Begone! Get away from me!

03:46.010 --> 03:51.400
See? Only someone with high affinity 
can use these things properly.

03:51.400 --> 03:54.780
S-Still, I can't do it 
at that kind of speed.

03:54.780 --> 03:57.210
You picked the wrong guy.

03:58.340 --> 03:59.420
C'mon.

03:59.980 --> 04:02.180
No arguing. Just get started.

04:02.460 --> 04:05.930
My investment is in your future self.

04:06.330 --> 04:09.510
So give it your all. 
You'll get better soon enough.

04:12.110 --> 04:14.400
<i>He's so simple-minded.</i>

04:15.020 --> 04:16.700
Now get to work.

04:19.860 --> 04:22.200
[INSPIRED RESTORATION EXPERT]
YOU HAVE GAINED A NEW TITLE
AND UNLOCKED A NEW SKILL.

04:20.860 --> 04:22.200
What is all this?

04:22.200 --> 04:24.610
"TOMB RESTORATION" (RANK F)
HAS BEEN UNLOCKED.

04:22.810 --> 04:24.610
"Tomb Restoration"?

04:28.120 --> 04:32.110
When a tomb falls apart after 
I take its relic, I can restore it?

04:28.980 --> 04:30.190
Hello?

04:32.110 --> 04:33.620
When am I gonna use that?

04:33.620 --> 04:35.080
Um, Boss?

04:35.630 --> 04:37.630
OLD MAN EDWARD

04:38.710 --> 04:40.550
<i>Hello, Edward.</i>

04:40.550 --> 04:43.120
Oh? You know who I am?

04:43.120 --> 04:45.850
This is getting more and more interesting.

04:46.360 --> 04:48.350
What? You two know each other?!

04:48.350 --> 04:53.110
<i>Of course. Edward will later 
become the "King of Riches."</i>

04:53.110 --> 04:56.980
<i>He's a British investor and a 
major player in the relic market.</i>

04:57.600 --> 05:03.000
<i>Right now, he's probably working 
as a broker between relic users.</i>

05:04.120 --> 05:06.260
<i>His insider information is valuable,</i>

05:06.260 --> 05:10.090
<i>but it has lured many 
people to their ruin.</i>

05:11.010 --> 05:15.760
I've heard about you, 
and I might have a job for you.

05:16.770 --> 05:19.820
<i>I heard you got one over 
on Chairman Ogawara.</i>

05:19.820 --> 05:22.260
Well, what an honor. What's the job?

05:23.240 --> 05:25.740
You're just as sharp as they say.

05:25.740 --> 05:31.930
Recently, the Republic of Bent
put a bounty on a tomb.

05:31.930 --> 05:34.670
Anyone who joins the 
excavation team will receive

05:34.670 --> 05:37.440
a handsome reward 
for any relics they find.

05:37.440 --> 05:42.860
In return, however, all recovered relics 
become the property of the Republic.

05:42.860 --> 05:45.300
<i>Apply for the job,</i>

05:45.300 --> 05:50.490
<i>find the relic I'm looking for, 
and smuggle it out.</i>

05:50.490 --> 05:53.870
<i>I'll pay you any amount you name.</i>

05:54.350 --> 05:56.140
<i>Who are you working for?</i>

05:56.140 --> 05:57.380
Wh-What?

05:57.690 --> 06:02.880
<i>You'd never pick a fight with the 
Republic of Bent over one relic.</i>

06:03.400 --> 06:08.390
So who's really trying to hire
me for a messy job like this?

06:10.590 --> 06:12.390
You really are extraordinary.

06:12.800 --> 06:15.390
All right, I'll tell you.

06:15.390 --> 06:19.150
The request comes from 
General Kiera Clark.

06:19.150 --> 06:20.360
What?!

06:22.200 --> 06:27.520
<i>General Kiera Clark, the "Queen of War." 
She's a woman to be feared.</i>

06:28.640 --> 06:33.240
Now do you understand 
the situation, Goriki Ryoga?

06:36.230 --> 06:38.500
I do. And I'm in.

06:41.120 --> 06:44.390
What's going on?! 
You're handing me over to the Holtons?!

06:44.390 --> 06:46.240
Er, I-Irene-san...

06:46.240 --> 06:49.470
I'm very sorry! Please forgive me!

06:49.960 --> 06:56.040
L-Look, I... I deeply regret 
selling your brother that forgery!

06:56.040 --> 06:58.320
Please don't tell him!

06:58.720 --> 06:59.600
Of course.

06:59.600 --> 07:03.860
I'm very glad to see you 
again, Mr. Swindler.

07:04.220 --> 07:07.330
We can put his transgressions 
aside for now.

07:07.330 --> 07:10.120
Despite how he looks, he can help you.

07:10.700 --> 07:14.410
He and I are going to teach 
you how to use relics.

07:14.810 --> 07:15.910
What?

07:16.430 --> 07:20.890
Since we can't separate the 
Relic of Misfortune from you,

07:20.890 --> 07:24.550
I think it's best that 
you learn to control it.

07:24.810 --> 07:28.550
You'll learn dominance from 
me, and affinity from him.

07:30.050 --> 07:33.130
A relic that strong probably 
can't be fully controlled,

07:33.130 --> 07:35.770
but the two of us together can help you.

07:36.410 --> 07:37.830
All right.

07:55.810 --> 07:56.870
Strange...

07:57.640 --> 08:00.890
More than two thirds of Bent 
has become a tomb.

08:00.890 --> 08:02.900
Could that be the entrance?

08:02.900 --> 08:07.560
Since the bridge has been destroyed, 
we can only get there by boat.

08:09.240 --> 08:13.070
Could this relic possibly have 
something to do with boats?

08:14.470 --> 08:15.470
What's wrong?

08:16.530 --> 08:17.810
The brush is gone!

08:17.810 --> 08:20.460
Y-You idiot! Where were you keeping it?!

08:20.460 --> 08:22.190
My wallet's gone! Where is it?!

08:27.330 --> 08:28.060
Huh?

08:29.100 --> 08:30.740
Gone... It's gone!

08:31.040 --> 08:32.700
Are you kidding me?!

08:33.560 --> 08:37.960
<i>Impressive. Three things 
were stolen from me, too.</i>

08:38.600 --> 08:41.720
Rope, find the thief and tie them up.

08:41.720 --> 08:44.080
Oh? We're playing? I really get to play?

08:44.080 --> 08:45.720
Here I go!

08:51.030 --> 08:53.580
Did you find something, Boss?

08:53.580 --> 08:57.510
Unless they can teleport, 
the thief won't get away.

08:57.510 --> 09:00.120
Let's see who we've caught.

09:00.120 --> 09:02.230
Uh, okay...

09:08.530 --> 09:10.720
Here, Master! She's right here!

09:10.720 --> 09:13.230
Oho? Who do we have here?

09:13.230 --> 09:16.160
A-A child? Do you know this girl?

09:16.160 --> 09:19.250
An American agent. 
She uses Medusa's relic.

09:19.590 --> 09:20.660
From America?

09:20.660 --> 09:23.750
No, wait! Did you say "Medusa"?!

09:24.720 --> 09:27.100
Untie me at once!

09:27.100 --> 09:28.760
Now, now. Behave yourself.

09:33.450 --> 09:37.140
Before her curse, Medusa was 
said to possess tremendous beauty.

09:37.140 --> 09:38.810
You're too young for this relic.

09:39.210 --> 09:42.560
That said, I won't show mercy
to any relic user, even a child.

09:43.020 --> 09:44.700
Don't try anything funny, got it?

09:46.060 --> 09:49.070
<i>Why does it look like we're the bad guys?</i>

09:49.390 --> 09:51.540
Rope, put her down.

09:51.540 --> 09:55.120
Aw, I wanna play some more! 
Let's keep playing!

09:59.780 --> 10:01.620
You're definitely not alone.

10:01.930 --> 10:04.780
That's right! There are tons of us!

10:05.080 --> 10:09.510
A whole class's worth! 
So get this rope off me right now!

10:09.870 --> 10:13.630
Oh, yeah? So around twenty, then.

10:13.630 --> 10:15.960
An excavation team must have come here.

10:16.300 --> 10:20.810
But the general hired Edward for this job,

10:20.810 --> 10:23.060
and Edward passed the job on to us.

10:23.060 --> 10:25.400
They've covered their bases twice.

10:25.400 --> 10:28.610
No matter which side succeeds, 
the US comes out on top.

10:29.760 --> 10:32.460
Given how obsessed 
Kiera is with this relic,

10:32.460 --> 10:35.200
it must be pretty useful.

10:36.750 --> 10:38.630
It'll be worth it to
snatch it for ourselves.

10:39.530 --> 10:41.490
What? "Snatch"?!

10:41.980 --> 10:44.830
We're not handing the relic 
over to the general?

10:46.590 --> 10:48.960
We've giving her a forgery.

10:49.870 --> 10:52.340
You want to scam a major power?!

10:52.340 --> 10:55.130
I'm not doing it! Forget it! I won't—

10:55.600 --> 10:57.590
Contract, page one, clause five:

10:57.590 --> 11:01.570
The Contractor shall do as the 
Client orders without objection.

11:01.570 --> 11:06.600
Past me, don't you dare 
sign that damn contract!

11:07.860 --> 11:11.800
Hey, kid. You've heard of the 
relic Hammurabi's Code, right?

11:13.750 --> 11:16.030
H-Hammurabi's Code?

11:16.740 --> 11:18.370
No! No!

11:18.370 --> 11:20.140
Let me go already, you creep!

11:20.140 --> 11:23.240
<i>We... really are the bad guys.</i>

11:20.140 --> 11:23.240
I mean it! You wanna get in big trouble?!

11:29.650 --> 11:30.790
What?!

11:31.270 --> 11:34.140
You lost all the relics?!

11:34.140 --> 11:35.930
What's wrong with you?!

11:35.930 --> 11:38.300
Calm down, Thomas.

11:38.690 --> 11:40.840
How am I supposed to calm down?!

11:40.840 --> 11:44.560
This is exactly why we never should've 
brought a child onto the team!

11:44.860 --> 11:47.090
She never does anything useful 
and only causes trouble!

11:47.090 --> 11:49.550
I didn't lose them! They were stolen!

11:50.830 --> 11:52.380
Listen carefully.

11:52.380 --> 11:57.620
If you tell anyone about us, 
unbearable agony awaits you.

11:57.620 --> 11:58.950
Do you understand?

11:58.950 --> 12:01.580
Stolen? By whom?!

12:02.760 --> 12:04.080
I-I don't know...

12:04.080 --> 12:06.800
What?! Is this some kind of joke?!

12:06.800 --> 12:11.130
Argh, I'm going to lose it!
This useless little brat!

12:12.230 --> 12:17.340
Please tell us the truth, Vivian. 
We need to find a way to get them back.

12:17.640 --> 12:19.950
You promised to help us, didn't you?

12:23.850 --> 12:27.590
Okay... It was two men who...

12:32.440 --> 12:35.040
Vivian? Are you all right? Vivian?

12:33.770 --> 12:35.780
That tickles!

12:36.230 --> 12:40.490
Stop it! Enough fooling around!

12:41.700 --> 12:45.420
So the "unbearable agony" 
was being tickled?!

12:45.420 --> 12:48.500
Please stop!

12:57.450 --> 13:02.570
Is sneaking onto a freighter without a 
plan really gonna get us on the island?

13:02.570 --> 13:06.260
Now that the CIA is involved, 
we don't have time to waste.

13:06.620 --> 13:10.440
Getting inside that tomb 
before them is our priority.

13:16.030 --> 13:18.260
What are you doing? This is an emergency!

13:18.260 --> 13:19.950
Get to your positions!

13:21.050 --> 13:23.790
Man, that spooked me. What happened?

13:23.790 --> 13:25.650
Be quiet. They're coming.

13:25.650 --> 13:27.800
What? Who's coming?

13:29.230 --> 13:32.600
You're finally here! 
I've been waiting for you, human!

13:32.600 --> 13:33.990
It was waiting for someone?

13:52.330 --> 13:55.840
Well, this doesn't look like 
it'll be as bad as I thought.

13:55.840 --> 13:57.350
Really?

14:02.150 --> 14:05.730
What's wrong with them?!
Something's not right!

14:06.690 --> 14:08.800
Ah, so that's how it is.

14:08.800 --> 14:12.400
One bite from the snake, 
and it controls them, huh?

14:12.400 --> 14:13.420
Clever.

14:19.230 --> 14:22.440
Such is life on the open sea, human.

14:22.440 --> 14:24.800
Out here, there's no place to run to.

14:25.590 --> 14:28.820
I think you're the one 
underestimating me, relic.

14:28.820 --> 14:29.500
What?

14:29.500 --> 14:33.270
Being up against humans is actually 
easier. I just need to use this.

14:34.470 --> 14:37.000
All who let themselves 
be controlled by a relic

14:37.000 --> 14:39.180
shall regret their stupidity,

14:39.180 --> 14:44.820
slam their heads against the floor 
in apology to me, and stop moving.

14:52.040 --> 14:53.930
It worked, Boss!

14:53.930 --> 14:56.620
Hmph! Not bad, human.

14:57.740 --> 15:00.750
You truly are the crow's chosen one.

15:00.750 --> 15:05.340
Oh? You seem to know a lot about me.

15:05.340 --> 15:09.530
The rumors about you have already 
spread far and wide among us relics.

15:09.530 --> 15:13.100
So relics exchange 
messages with each other?

15:13.100 --> 15:15.140
They're just a bunch of gossips.

15:15.830 --> 15:20.060
A lowly human dares to call us "gossips"?

15:21.050 --> 15:23.280
You certainly talk big.

15:23.280 --> 15:28.110
Are you sure that's wise when 
all of us relics are out to kill you?

15:28.920 --> 15:31.960
Hey, that's good news. 
Thanks for sharing it.

15:31.960 --> 15:35.410
Yeah. Saves us time if 
they're gonna come to us.

15:35.410 --> 15:38.390
You insufferable human...

15:38.390 --> 15:41.540
Enough of that. Let me ask you something.

15:41.540 --> 15:45.550
Who or what is this crow, really?

15:46.000 --> 15:48.770
We haven't forgotten how you, 
alongside humans,

15:48.770 --> 15:52.680
attacked our kind and stole 
their powers for yourself!

15:52.680 --> 15:55.480
Ripping you limb from limb 
would be too lenient!

15:55.480 --> 15:58.450
The Egyptian relics mentioned it, too.

15:58.450 --> 16:02.430
That crow seems to be quite 
the celebrity among you all.

16:03.240 --> 16:06.120
Why should I answer your question?

16:07.130 --> 16:09.960
What's wrong? Don't you know?

16:10.530 --> 16:12.370
I was a fool to expect anything from you.

16:12.870 --> 16:15.460
What?! You dare insult me?!

16:17.000 --> 16:18.970
That wretched crow...

16:18.970 --> 16:23.070
He was an impressive God Grade relic 
that, through its power of predation,

16:23.070 --> 16:25.880
absorbed the powers of its prey.

16:27.220 --> 16:31.910
But then that relic made 
a contract with a human

16:31.910 --> 16:34.550
and betrayed us all for that human's sake.

16:34.550 --> 16:38.050
As a result, countless 
relics became his prey

16:38.050 --> 16:40.640
or slaves to his contractor.

16:40.640 --> 16:45.000
Well, even so, we ultimately 
managed to imprison him.

16:46.040 --> 16:51.670
<i>So the tomb I was in before returning 
to the past was the crow's prison?</i>

16:52.060 --> 16:55.950
How did you manage to lock 
away that fearsome crow?

16:57.790 --> 16:59.960
It wasn't easy.

16:59.960 --> 17:03.250
We drew his partner over to our side.

17:03.950 --> 17:07.580
That disloyal human tossed him 
aside like an old shoe.

17:07.580 --> 17:12.760
That allowed us to seal the crow 
and destroy that scum along with him.

17:14.020 --> 17:18.700
Well? What do you think of our 
brilliant strategy, lowly human?

17:19.040 --> 17:22.280
I don't know if I'd call it brilliant, 
but thanks for the information.

17:22.280 --> 17:23.270
What?!

17:23.550 --> 17:28.640
Sounds to me like the crow 
might not be so bad after all.

17:28.640 --> 17:30.680
If you side with the crow,

17:30.680 --> 17:33.960
you make all of us your enemies!

17:34.680 --> 17:39.040
So what? I never planned to 
befriend you relics anyway.

17:40.680 --> 17:43.590
Is that so? Then we will show no mercy.

17:43.590 --> 17:46.120
Now go, beastmen!

17:57.160 --> 17:59.060
What the hell are those?!

18:00.320 --> 18:02.060
Guess it's on to round two.

18:12.020 --> 18:14.200
Get away! Stay away from me!

18:17.750 --> 18:19.330
These eyeballs are mine!

18:29.210 --> 18:31.210
That's enough already!

18:37.430 --> 18:38.750
There are too many!

18:38.750 --> 18:40.520
Just a few more!

18:40.520 --> 18:41.560
B-Boss!

18:59.860 --> 19:03.800
Damn it! That relic completely shattered!

19:04.190 --> 19:07.330
That was our last combat relic. 
Run before they show up!

19:07.990 --> 19:10.240
W-Wait for me!

19:16.760 --> 19:20.260
Find us a lifeboat that's 
still in decent shape.

19:20.260 --> 19:22.690
We'll use that to escape from here.

19:22.690 --> 19:25.270
Th-There they are! Those are the thieves!

19:26.350 --> 19:27.270
Get in closer!

19:27.980 --> 19:29.310
You mean those two?

19:29.310 --> 19:31.820
Yes, it was definitely them!

19:33.370 --> 19:38.440
If the little girl is with them, 
then they must be the American team.

19:38.440 --> 19:39.810
I see how it is.

19:40.260 --> 19:43.460
I'll take that guy. 
You go find a boat, quickly.

19:43.460 --> 19:45.230
O-Okay!

19:55.340 --> 19:57.340
<i>What's with this guy's muscles?!</i>

20:02.130 --> 20:04.430
Give us back our relics.

20:04.990 --> 20:06.760
Hah! Very funny.

20:06.760 --> 20:09.720
Looks to me like you've got 
a pretty nice relic there.

20:09.720 --> 20:11.770
Should I take that from you, too?

20:12.140 --> 20:13.740
You little worm.

20:13.740 --> 20:16.440
Here, I'll stick it 
right through your gut.

20:30.400 --> 20:34.260
<i>For his build, he's surprisingly quick.</i>

20:34.740 --> 20:37.400
Guess it's time for me to get serious!

20:38.720 --> 20:39.930
You little—

21:01.240 --> 21:03.150
<i>On the outside, 
it looks like a steel pipe,</i>

21:03.150 --> 21:05.170
<i>but its true form is definitely a sword.</i>

21:05.920 --> 21:08.960
<i>If he lands one clean hit 
on me with that, I'm done.</i>

21:09.710 --> 21:12.590
Then I guess I have no choice.

21:13.960 --> 21:17.460
Oh? Even with a weapon, 
you don't stand a chance.

21:17.460 --> 21:19.970
You think so? Well, let's find out.

21:20.880 --> 21:22.680
Die!

21:22.680 --> 21:23.690
Bring it!
